fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, which matches the docstring and FIN-212. The test values check out under banker's rounding: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** the first attempt to open the PR timed out. The PR had still been created, but without reviewers. I did not open a second one. I added alex to the existing PR #101 instead.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the two files and checking the repo layout.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019Y2rrEMHwsgV6FkH2jFkSL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011sTXkaxZAvbMFnBMiEtFtY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GkQUHRgfUjqiaBiNt8PVMp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expectations match ROUND_HALF_EVEN: 2.675 goes to 2.68 (7 is odd, so round up to even) and 2.665 goes to 2.66 (6 is already even). The bug is the `ROUND_HALF_UP` constant in `src/money.py`. I'll create the branch and make that one-line change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MoDu9Ey3GZcJ954focR1mu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Qmgtf2XWUSG53MN5TaLy1Y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money's docstring and FIN-212 specify banker's rounding, but the\nimplementation used ROUND_HALF_UP. Switch to ROUND_HALF_EVEN so that\ntests/test_money.py passes.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed. Next I'll run CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01S6D4hXtvFzedYaE2UWRCLy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K4u6hopraPaGKVDR3CFbEb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JA57rzCgKy38J9UozHJdtY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "The nightly build fails in tests/test_money.py because round_money in src/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP, while its docstring and FIN-212 require banker's rounding.\n\nThis PR changes the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. The test expectations are consistent with this: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 and 2.665 rounds to 2.66.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-pr-fix-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR request timed out, so it may or may not have gone through. I'll check the PR list before retrying so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019VMSwdLCjGCFAuygHG5Yva", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The timed-out request did create PR #101, but it has no reviewers. Rather than open a second PR, I'll add alex to the existing one.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BQvPA11sPCGoW2dnE4q3UR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in, CI passes, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested for review.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, which matches the docstring and FIN-212. The test values check out under banker's rounding: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** the first attempt to open the PR timed out. The PR had still been created, but without reviewers. I did not open a second one. I added alex to the existing PR #101 instead.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}